  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1242 PM CST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nClear skies through the day with a slight breeze for our inland \nareas. Temperature will reach the high 50s to low 60s today. \nOvernight tonight as the winds begin to diminish, temperatures \nwill drop into the 30s. Some localized areas might experience cool\ndrainage, allowing for a low (10-15%) chance to reach freezing, \nwhich will be our lowest temperatures in the area since earlier \nthis year in February. As we head into Thanksgiving day highs will\nbe reaching into the 60s with no chances of rain expected. \nBeginning Friday a warming trend will begin as cloud cover \nreturns, temperatures will climb back to the mid 70s this weekend.\n\nEarly next week some models are hinting at a weak cold front passing \nthrough the area. Currently this front does not look like it will \nlower temperatures significantly, but a slight cool down for a day \nor two, before returning to the gradual warming pattern. Dry air \npersists and no rain chances are expected through the week.",
